<title>SWEDEN: Hufvudstaden to list international unit.</title>
<headline>Hufvudstaden to list international unit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish property company Hufvudstadet said on Tuesday it planned to launch a share buy-back programme totalling 2.87 billion crowns and to list its international unit on the Stockholm bourse.  </p>
<p>Hufvudstaden said the programme would mean a considerable recapitalisation for the company and shareholders would realise part of the surplus value of Swedish property holdings.</p>
<p>-- Simon Haydon, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
